Brute method : (using STACK)
class Solution {
    public ListNode reverseList(ListNode head) {

        ListNode temp = head;
        Stack<Integer> st = new Stack<>();

        while (temp != null) {
            st.push(temp.val);      // Push all node values into the stack
            temp = temp.next;
        }

        temp = head;                // Start again from the head

        while (temp != null) {
            temp.val = st.pop();    // Pop the top value and assign it
            temp = temp.next;
        }

        return head;
    }
}
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(n) (because of the stack)


Optimal: 
class Solution {
    public ListNode reverseList(ListNode head) {

        ListNode temp = head;              // Start traversing from the head
        ListNode prev = null;              // Previous node is initially null

        while (temp != null) {             // Traverse until the end of the list

            ListNode front = temp.next;    // Store the next node before changing the link

            temp.next = prev;              // Reverse the current node's link

            prev = temp;                   // Move prev one step forward

            temp = front;                  // Move temp to the next node (saved in front)
        }

        return prev;                       // Prev becomes the new head after reversal
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
// REMEMBER:
temp  → Current node
prev  → Previous node
front → Next node (saved before breaking the link)

1. Save the next node.
2. Reverse the current node's link.
3. Move prev forward.
4. Move temp forward.
5. Repeat.
